<section aria-labelledby="brands">
  <h2 id="brands">2. Brands</h2>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_name) %>">2.1 Brand name</h3>
  <p>
    Write the brand name as the brand uses it in its own texts, for example in manuals, in
    brochures or on the "About" page of its website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Example: <i>Fezz Audio</i>. The logo only shows <i>Fezz</i>, but the brand calls itself
    <i>Fezz Audio</i> in its texts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not use a shorter form, for example from the logo, and do not use the registered company
    name (see <a href="#<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_legal_name) %>">2.3</a>).
  </p>
  <p>
    Use the same capitals and special characters as the brand: <i>DeVORE Fidelity</i>,
    <i>Bang &amp; Olufsen</i>. Do not "correct" the spelling of a brand.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_abbreviation) %>">2.2 Abbreviation</h3>
  <p>
    Only fill in the abbreviation if the brand is often known by a short form that is <b>not</b>
    part of its name: <i>B&amp;O</i> for <i>Bang &amp; Olufsen</i>, <i>AAT</i> for
    <i>Advanced Audio Technologies</i>. The abbreviation lets users find these brands when they search
    for the short form.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      There is nothing to add for <i>Fezz Audio</i> or <i>DeVORE Fidelity</i>: a search for
      <i>Fezz</i> or <i>DeVORE</i> already finds them by the brand name. You don't have to add an
      abbreviation like "Fezz" or "DeVORE" in this case.
    </li>
    <li>
      There is also nothing to add when the brand name <i>is</i> the abbreviation and the letters are
      only history. <i>KEF</i> was founded in the buildings of <i>Kent Engineering &amp; Foundry</i>,
      <i>NAD</i> stands for <i>New Acoustic Dimension</i>. Nobody uses these long forms, so leave the
      field empty and write the history in the description.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_legal_name) %>">2.3 Registered company name</h3>
  <p>
    The legal name of the company, with its suffix, for example <i>Bang &amp; Olufsen AS</i>.
    Leave it empty if it is the same as the brand name.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_details) %>">2.4 Founded, discontinued and country</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The country is where the brand is headquartered now. It is not where the products are made.</li>
    <li>For a discontinued brand, use the country where it was headquartered last.</li>
    <li>If the brand moved to another country, write about the move in the description.</li>
    <li>A brand is discontinued when it no longer releases or sells new products.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_categories) %>">2.5 Categories</h3>
  <p>
    Categories are added to a brand automatically from the categories of its products. You only
    have to select categories for a brand that has no products on HiFi&thinsp;Log yet.
  </p>

  <h3 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:brand_ownership) %>">2.6 New owners</h3>
  <p>
    If another company buys a brand and it continues with the same name, it stays one brand on
    HiFi&thinsp;Log. Write the owners and the dates in the description.
  </p>
</section>
